---
import Portrait from './Portrait.astro';
import Review from './Review.astro';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
import { speakerPortrait } from '../config/assets';

const ledger = [
  { k: 'Team USA', v: 'Four-time Team USA athlete' },
  { k: 'National titles', v: 'Two-time national triathlon champion' },
  { k: 'Ironman', v: 'Ironman finisher' },
  { k: 'Skydives', v: 'More than 3,000' },
  { k: 'Profession', v: 'Senior Producer, Publicis' },
];
---
<section id="speaker" class="relative bg-paper py-24 md:py-36" aria-labelledby="speaker-title">
  <div class="wrap grid grid-cols-4 gap-x-5 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-x-6">
    <SectionHead index="04" label="The Speaker" />

    <div class="reveal col-span-4 md:col-span-5 md:row-span-3">
      <div class="aspect-[4/5] overflow-hidden rounded-3xl md:sticky md:top-28 [&_img]:object-[50%_20%]">
        <Portrait photo={speakerPortrait} slot="Speaker portrait — Cameron Schiller" spec="Portrait 4:5 · B&W · ≥ 2000 px" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 40vw, 100vw" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-4 mt-12 md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 md:mt-0">
      <h2 id="speaker-title" class="display text-[17vw] uppercase md:text-[6.6vw] 2xl:text-[6.5rem]">
        <span class="reveal block">Cameron</span>
        <span class="reveal block" style="--d:80ms">Schiller</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="reveal label mt-6 text-ash" style="--d:160ms">Speaker · Team USA Athlete · Creative Leader</p>

      <p class="reveal lede mt-12 text-[1.75rem] md:text-[2.1rem]">Cameron Schiller knows what it means to redefine normal.</p>
      <div class="reveal mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
        <p>Five years ago, Cameron Schiller was 60 pounds overweight, had no background in endurance sports, and had no money to his name.</p>
        <p>Today, he’s a two-time national triathlon champion, an Ironman athlete, and entering his fourth year representing Team USA.</p>
        <p>But his transformation didn’t stop at athletics.</p>
        <p>Cameron applied the same principles to rebuilding his professional career, becoming a Senior Producer at Publicis, where he leads large-scale global productions for some of the world’s most recognized brands.</p>
        <p>Those experiences became the foundation of the Operator-Athlete Method—an approach to developing the capabilities that make extraordinary transformation possible.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="col-span-4 mt-14 md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 md:mt-14" aria-label="Selected background">
      {ledger.map((row, i) => (
        <div class="reveal grid grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr] gap-4 border-t border-line-ink py-4 last:border-b" style={`--d:${i * 60}ms`}>
          <dt class="label pt-1 text-ash">{row.k}</dt>
          <dd class="text-lg">{row.verify ? <Review note="Verify">{row.v}</Review> : row.v}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <div class="col-span-4 mt-12 md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7">
      <details class="group border-t border-ink">
        <summary class="label flex min-h-14 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between py-4 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="group-open:hidden">Read the full biography</span>
          <span class="hidden group-open:inline">Close biography</span>
          <span class="text-lg transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="space-y-5 pb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
          <p>Five years ago, Cameron Schiller was 60 pounds overweight, had no background in endurance sports, and had no money to his name. The life he leads today would have seemed extraordinary to the person he was then.</p>
          <p>Through commitment, coaching, disciplined action, and a willingness to enter unfamiliar environments, Cameron transformed himself into a two-time national triathlon champion, an Ironman athlete, and a four-time Team USA representative.</p>
          <p>But the most significant transformation wasn’t simply physical.</p>
          <p>Cameron began to recognize that the principles helping him develop extraordinary athletic capabilities could be applied far beyond sport.</p>
          <p>He took those lessons into rebuilding his professional career, becoming a Senior Producer at Publicis. Today, he leads complex, large-scale global productions for brands including Toyota’s Paris 2024 Olympic Games campaign, Heineken, Verizon, Marriott Bonvoy, and Tide.</p>
          <p>With more than 3,000 skydives, years of endurance competition, and experience leading high-stakes international productions, Cameron has developed a perspective on the relationship between preparation, commitment, adaptability, trust, and performance.</p>
          <p class="text-ink">These experiences form the foundation of the Operator-Athlete Method, his approach to understanding how people develop new capabilities and change what they believe is possible.</p>
          <p>Through Redefine Normal, Cameron shares the experiences and principles behind his transformation, inviting audiences to reconsider their own limitations and begin developing the capabilities to move beyond them.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
